# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-safe-recoveries.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/379-reject-non-canonical-spec-file-s-before-worker-dispatch/requirements.md
Feature: Reject non-canonical spec File(s) before worker dispatch
  The publication File(s) parser previously rejected prose only after execute
  dispatched the implement worker, and reported only publication_scope_unproven.
  This was fixed by sharing one grammar, failing closed before panes and
  spec-created, locating diagnostics, and rewriting recoverable existing
  packages only through approved upgrade.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Invalid prose is rejected before workers
    Given an Approved spec whose delivery task declares File(s) Create `src/a.ts`
    When spec validation or execute controller preflight runs
    Then the issue is not treated as executable
    And no pane or worker is created
    And the failure is publication_scope_unproven with spec path, task ID, line, exact invalid entry, and accepted syntax

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Canonical literal path binds
    Given an Approved spec whose delivery task declares only File(s) `src/a.ts`
    When publication scope is bound
    Then the allowed-path set contains only that path plus spec-owned paths

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Bounded glob or directory for generated steps
    Given a documented bounded repository-relative glob or directory declaration for generated BDD step files
    When publication scope is bound
    Then matching files under that declaration are authorized
    And unrelated files remain unauthorized

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Write-spec and public documentation use the parser grammar
    Given /sdlc-write-spec is producing an Approved tasks.md and a user consults README.md
    When the installed publication File(s) parser reads every delivery-task File(s) line
    Then every declaration is accepted by that parser
    And README documents the canonical grammar, prose rejection, and pre-dispatch diagnostics

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: No regression of valid declarations
    Given currently valid quoted paths, comma/semicolon lists, globs, directories, and delivery-owner-only annotations
    When the grammar is shared and the new gates run
    Then those cases remain green
    And authorization stays fail-closed

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Upgrade rewrites recoverable existing File(s)
    Given an issue-owned tasks.md whose delivery File(s) is Create `src/a.ts`
    When /sdlc-upgrade-project detects and the operator approves publication-files
    Then the line is rewritten to File(s) `src/a.ts`
    And the live parser still rejects the original prose without that rewrite
    And mixed unsafe quoted spans remain findings without mutation

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Initial nonzero smoke execute remains failed without exact proof
    Given the registered smoke provider persisted its immutable original baseline and retained invocation outside the checkout
    When the nested execute exits nonzero without exact same-run delivery proof
    Then the provider remains failed
    And it does not launch a replacement issue or clone

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Same outer run accepts exact controller-owned recovery
    Given the original nested run later records same-issue and same-PR post-merge recovery at a final head
    And the original verified head is an ancestor of that final head
    And current verification, identity-bound recovery-session delivery, and delivery proof evidence match
    When the same stable outer verification run reruns with only report evidence dirtiness changed
    Then the original nonzero invocation passes from a new baseline-excluded exact-head merged PR and closed issue
    And no replacement queue is launched

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Recovered smoke evidence is fail closed
    Given the original smoke invocation is retained after nonzero exit
    When its <evidence> is missing, stale, malformed, or mismatched
    Then recovery remains failed without a new clone or issue
    Examples:
      | evidence |
      | nested run identity |
      | issue or pull request identity |
      | expected or final head ancestry |
      | original closing-PR baseline |
      | validation ID or config |
      | verification artifact |
      | recovery session handoff |

  @SCN010 @regression
  Scenario: Separate token authenticates nested recursion suppression
    Given nested delivery proof generation retains NMG_SDLC_SMOKE_OWNED equal to 1
    When the verify pane receives the provider-created recovery token
    Then recursion suppression validates the token against the exact clone and nested run
    And a bare or mismatched ownership environment fails

  @SCN011 @regression
  Scenario: Terminal proof is replayed without a retained clone
    Given exact reconciliation persisted immutable cleanup-pending proof before deleting the clone
    When cleanup succeeds and the same stable outer run invokes the provider again
    Then the state is terminal-clean and the stored issue, PR, final head, and original baseline are revalidated remotely
    And no clone, baseline, execute queue, or replacement issue is created
    And cleanup failure remains incomplete and a rerun retries only cleanup

  @SCN012 @regression
  Scenario: Ordinary success binds proof to nested run identity
    Given nested execute exits zero and cleanup may remove run.json
    When smoke delivery proof is evaluated
    Then every issue proof has one delivery-helper-authored run ID and exact PR and head
    And a present invalid or mismatched run.json fails instead of falling back to proof-only identity

  @SCN013 @regression
  Scenario: Exact pre-store smoke failure upgrades into retained recovery
    Given stable outer run #379 has no external recovery-store record
    And its current verification JSON contains one failed repository.nmg-sdlc-smoke result for configured issue #109
    And that result contains one allowlisted retained clone, one complete #109 baseline command, and one nonzero execute command
    And the retained clone has no smoke-deliveries proof but has the failed root deliver handoff, exact nested run and expected head, current passed verification JSON artifact, matched passed recovery-session handoff, and consumed post_merge_observation
    When the provider reruns for the same stable outer issue, project, spec, validation, config, and queue
    Then it atomically seeds the failed recovery record
    And it accepts only the baseline-excluded remote exact PR and head as MERGED with #109 CLOSED
    And it does not clone, execute, or launch a replacement issue

  @SCN014 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Pre-store migration rejects ambiguity and tampering
    Given stable outer run #379 has no external recovery-store record
    And otherwise-valid Markdown verification cannot substitute for the nested JSON artifact
    When its current outer verification JSON has <defect>
    Then no recovery record is seeded
    And no replacement clone, execute queue, or issue is launched
    Examples:
      | defect |
      | duplicate retained-clone artifacts |
      | incomplete or duplicate baseline commands |
      | duplicate or mismatched execute evidence |
      | mismatched validation config or issue queue |
      | tampered outer artifact identity |

  @SCN015 @regression
  Scenario: Recovery-store lock cleanup belongs only to the owner
    Given one smoke recovery writer holds the exclusive state lock
    When another writer fails to acquire that lock
    Then the owner's lock remains and a subsequent writer is still blocked
    And after the owner releases and cleans up the lock the next atomic write succeeds
